{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:59:11Z","created_by_operation":"op_e17d59047d0042ca80734c14b4e77405","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_cf2a54ee6f4230ba40aa9f35c9c1979e36c325585884fee5ded7b00276fe16f6","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"agentsmesh/agentsmesh@1f90b14194d0 snapshot d9e238fa0886609c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_d8c10bb9caee4a5634b30265c4f4da7071bc41ebc961cc53dc3a4eb657bcb008"],"source_ids":["src_426d83554c51520fb75bd307c432fefb"],"text":"The stack uses PostgreSQL and Redis, MinIO for S3-compatible storage, Traefik as reverse proxy, JWT for web auth and mTLS for runner connections.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:59:11Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e17d59047d0042ca80734c14b4e77405"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:59:11Z","created_by_operation":"op_e17d59047d0042ca80734c14b4e77405","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_e207fcc2a48dcd22c6f07ea244a08c1a60ce2d472de05dc95c581712d7856e99","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"agentsmesh/agentsmesh@1f90b14194d0 snapshot d9e238fa0886609c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0f87a75b273d680e8bdb0c0a11985a0ef20bfb3c71827d957c7cf011a2272a81","slc_2fb17dcbca5670b22ca410774f2d3e508d9eecc1f26d8edc4802e17916e19d56"],"source_ids":["src_426d83554c51520fb75bd307c432fefb"],"text":"Any terminal-based agent can run; built-in support is documented for Claude Code, Codex CLI, Gemini CLI, Aider, and OpenCode.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:59:11Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e17d59047d0042ca80734c14b4e77405"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:59:11Z","created_by_operation":"op_e17d59047d0042ca80734c14b4e77405","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_ea545419cf54b28aff3267fb6248324edbe84867533bc99c44bde783790620b3","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"agentsmesh/agentsmesh@1f90b14194d0 snapshot d9e238fa0886609c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_f88ed077632bda278c065b63794dda573ccb1a53d8ad278a7edb549b89d158a6"],"source_ids":["src_426d83554c51520fb75bd307c432fefb"],"text":"Server side comprises a Go backend (Gin+GORM) handling auth, pod lifecycle, tickets, billing and runner-cert PKI; a WebSocket Relay for terminal data; and a self-hosted Go runner daemon that spawns PTY pods.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:59:11Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e17d59047d0042ca80734c14b4e77405"}
